33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found out that chasing small payments takes six hours a month! That's so much time. I think we should avoid any system that requires constant chasing.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The ledger shows that seventy percent of our costs are fixed. We cannot afford a flexible system that risks these basics. We need a guaranteed minimum.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,I've seen that mid-year joiners are hesitant when the math gets complicated. We should avoid a structure that makes people feel like they are being audited.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"I've got it! People are hesitating because they feel like they're being charged for every little thing. The ""pay-as-you-go"" vibe is killing the spontaneity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"How charming. While you're worried about ""vibes,"" the data shows a tiny minority is doing all the work and attending everything. It's a total imbalance.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, I agree. If we make it a simple yearly fee, it would be easier for the members and much, much easier for the treasurer.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"A single yearly fee is the most stable, but we must ensure the amount is high enough to cover those fixed costs without relying on ""hope.""","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"A single fee is good, but we must be careful not to make it so high that it scares off newcomers. It should be a low barrier to entry.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! If we just pay once and forget about it, people will stop weighing up whether it's ""worth it"" to come out for one evening.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,A flat fee just rewards the ghosts. Why should the people who actually run the place and use the facilities pay the same as someone who shows up twice?,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"But @Shunichi, if we make it too complex to punish the ""ghosts,"" the treasurer will spend all their time doing math instead of enjoying the club.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with Minato on the administrative side, but I agree with Shunichi that we can't ignore the cost. We need a figure that is mathematically sound.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"If we create tiers based on usage, we create a visible hierarchy. That will make the quieter members feel even more like outsiders.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Precisely. We want people to feel like they belong, not like they're paying for a subscription service. Let's make it effortless to just show up.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Effortless for whom? The ghosts? It's not ""belonging"" if you're just a name on a list. It's a free ride on the backs of the active members.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want everyone to be happy and for the treasurer to have their evenings back. A simple, single payment seems the most peaceful way.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Peace is a luxury. Financial solvency is a necessity. Whatever we choose, the total must cover the fixed costs with a reasonable buffer.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I believe the health of the club depends on its inclusivity. A flat, modest fee is the only way to ensure newcomers don't feel judged.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,Let's stop treating the club like a business. It's a social circle! Let's remove the barriers and get the energy back into the room.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm the only one here concerned with actual fairness. If we ignore the workload imbalance, we're just encouraging the active members to burn out.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
