60,3,1,talk,Minato,,I really prefer Option A. It's the simplest for everyone and it means the treasurer doesn't have to spend hours chasing small amounts of money.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A is the only one that provides the financial certainty I'm looking for. We can set a figure that covers the fixed costs without guesswork.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,I strongly support Option A. It avoids creating visible distinctions between members and ensures that newcomers can drift in without feeling scrutinized.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A is the only way to go! No more ""should I go tonight?"" calculations. You've paid, you belong, you just show up. It's perfect.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Of course you all love the easy way. Option A is a subsidy for the lazy. Option C is the only rational choice to address the imbalance of effort.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I understand it feels unfair, but is the ""fairness"" worth making the treasurer's life a nightmare? I'm worried about the burnout.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, Option C still requires a level of administration to track who is in which tier. Option A is the most logically sound for stability.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,Option C would essentially label people by their level of commitment. That is exactly the kind of atmosphere that pushes people away.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! Imagine the pressure of picking a ""tier."" It's like a commitment contract. It's the opposite of the welcoming vibe we need.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"You're all prioritizing ""vibes"" and ""convenience"" over actual justice. The people doing the work are the ones who will be most annoyed by Option A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I just think a peaceful club is a better club. If we make it simple, we can spend more time together and less time arguing about money.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I've looked at the numbers. The fixed costs are too high to risk with Option B, and Option C is too unstable. Option A is the only reasonable path.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,We must remember that the club's strength is its low-pressure environment. Option A preserves that. Option C destroys it by making participation a transaction.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"Let's just be honest: Option A is the most charming. It says ""you're part of the group, now come and have fun."" No strings attached.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"""No strings attached"" is just another way of saying ""the active members will keep doing all the work for free."" It's an absurd way to run a club.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm sorry you feel that way, Shunichi, but I really believe simplicity is the kindest choice for the person who has to manage the books.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"My priority is that we don't end up in a deficit. Option A allows us to set a firm, calculated figure that guarantees our survival.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I cannot support a system that creates a hierarchy of membership. For the sake of the newcomers and the quiet members, we must choose Option A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for the fun and the flow! Let's get rid of the hesitation and make it easy for everyone to just be here.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll stand my ground. If we don't acknowledge the disparity in contribution, we're just lying to ourselves. I'm voting for the only fair option.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
